  "notes": "Source: Official Luddy School B.S. in Informatics degree requirements (luddy.indianapolis.iu.edu/academics/undergraduate/informatics/requirements/index.html). The B.S. is a 120 credit hour program: Core A (53 cr.), Career Readiness (2 cr.), Core B (6 cr. of 300+ CSCI/INFO/LIS/NEWM), Capstone (3 cr.), General Education (21 cr.; Social Science and Analytical Reasoning List B fulfilled by the INFO Core), General Electives (14 cr.), and a required Area of Specialization (21 cr. - any minor, major, or certificate). Students must earn a C- or higher in all courses with a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Semester layout arranged in prerequisite order following the standard Informatics course sequence; the school's official interactive degree map (pathways.iu.edu) requires JavaScript and could not be transcribed, so term placement follows catalog course sequencing. Core B, Capstone, Specialization, and General Education blocks are modeled as constrained-choice slots. No courses, credits, or prereqs invented.",
